# admin wrote their own, which SOURCES the same helpers file, and named only that on the command
# line. The `.` is what takes custody (`rul-speaker-minting-is-oracle-sourcing-only`), so the
# admin's vouch may rest on helpers they did not write — because sourcing is the promise that they
# read them and answer for them.
#
# THE CONTRAST THAT MAKES THIS A PAIR. `pin28-helper-package-entrypoints-discarded` writes the
# replacement entrypoint IN THE BOOK instead, and it DECLINES: a book mints no speaker, not by
# co-loading and not by sourcing either. The difference between these two cells is where the
# replacement is written, and that is exactly the line the ruling draws — wanting somebody else's
